# Host canonicalization: apex -> www (requires both domains to be attached
# to the Cloudflare Pages project). Without this, the full site is served
# as duplicate content on https://elevategrowth.solutions.
https://elevategrowth.solutions/* https://www.elevategrowth.solutions/:splat 301

# 301 Redirects for old/changed URLs
/services/branding /services 301
/services/ad-campaigns /services 301
/meet-us /behind-elevate 301
/home / 301
/beginners-guide /blog 301
/pricing /services 301
/las-vegas-digital-marketing / 301

# NOTE (Cloudflare Pages behavior):
# - Every route, including each blog post, is prerendered to a flat
#   `<path>.html` file at build time (scripts/generate-seo-pages.mjs), so no
#   SPA fallback rewrite is needed. A `/blog/* /index.html 200` rewrite does
#   NOT work on Pages (/index.html itself redirects to /), which used to make
#   blog posts return 404.
# - Unmatched paths automatically serve 404.html with a real 404 status
#   because a top-level 404.html exists; a `/* /404.html 404` rule is
#   unsupported syntax on Pages and is not needed.
